==Version history==
It is originally granted from [[monster modifier]] [[Modifier:MonsterAuraAccuracyAndCrits1|{{c|mod|Accuracy and Crits Aura}}]] but the mod is spawn disabled since version 3.18.0. The aura was then granted by new [[Archnemesis]] monster mod {{ml|MonsterArchnemesisDeadeye}}  (rare rarity version only; also known as <span style="color:olive">Deadeye</span> in the text under the monster nameplate) from version 3.18 to 3.19 (the <span style="color:olive">Deadeye</span> version as league mechanic during game ver.3.17 (Archnemesis league) does not grants aura). The totem version probably introduced at the same time as the initial version, and later forked to be [[Modifier:MonsterImplicitAuraAccuracyAndCritsSextant|a mod]] for totem that spawn from sextant only. Sextants and their mod pool are removed from [[version 3.24.0]].

The Archnemesis version was much stronger than sextant totem version, which the Archnemesis' (<span style="color:olive">Deadeye</span>'s) Accuracy and Crits Aura grants {{c|mod|100% increased Global Accuracy Rating}} and  {{c|mod|100% increased Global Critical Strike Chance}}, as well as other effect that grant to the mod owner of the <span style="color:olive">Deadeye</span> mod.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3267228|title=What's Next for Archnemesis Modifiers
|author=Chris|date=May 15, 2022|accessdate=June 18, 2023|publisher=Official Path of Exile Forums}}</ref> While the totem spawned from the sextant mod, only grant {{c|mod|45% increased Global Accuracy Rating}} and {{c|mod|100% increased Global Critical Strike Chance}}, despite the totem also grants {{stl|Speed Aura}} buff. The current value of Accuracy and Crits Aura from the monster mod is not publicly announced and rely on datamining game files to deduce the values.

